[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 1. **Starting material: trans-cinnamaldehyde**
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - trans-cinnamaldehyde has the structure: C6H5-CH=CH-CHO
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Count the carbons:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85]   - Phenyl ring (C6H5): 6 carbons
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85]   - Vinyl unit (CH=CH): 2 carbons
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85]   - Aldehyde carbon (CHO): 1 carbon
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Total carbons: 6 + 2 + 1 = 9 carbons
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 2. **Step 1: Treatment with methylmagnesium bromide (Grignard reagent)**
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Methylmagnesium bromide (CH3MgBr) adds a methyl group to aldehydes or ketones, converting the carbonyl group to an alcohol.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The aldehyde (CHO) carbon is converted to a secondary alcohol with a new methyl group added.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The product (Product 1) will have an extra carbon from the methyl group.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - So, new carbon count = 9 + 1 = 10 carbons.
