[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 4. **Step 3: Product 3 was treated with (dimethyl(oxo)-l6-sulfaneylidene)methane in DMSO at elevated temperature, forming product 3**
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The compound (dimethyl(oxo)-l6-sulfaneylidene)methane is the IUPAC or systematic name for the reagent commonly known as dimethyl sulfoxonium methylide, which is a Wittig-type ylide used for epoxidation or cyclopropanation reactions.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - When treated with α,β-unsaturated ketones (like product 2), this methylene ylide typically performs cyclopropanation on the double bond.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The cyclopropanation adds a CH2 group to the double bond, converting the C=C into a cyclopropane ring.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The ylide (dimethyl(oxo)-l6-sulfaneylidene)methane has 1 carbon in its reactive moiety (the "methylene" carbon which is transferred).
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - So, carbon count of product 3 = carbon count of product 2 + 1 = 10 + 1 = 11 carbons.
