[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 问题: A coating is applied to a substrate resulting in a perfectly smooth surface. The measured contact angles of this smooth coating are 132° and 102° for water and hexadecane respectively. The coating formulation is then modified and when now applied to the same type of substrate, a rough surface is produced. When a droplet of water or oil sits on the rough surface, the wettability of the surface can now be described by the Cassie-Baxter state. The water contact angle on the rough surface is now 148°. What would be the best estimate of the contact angle of a droplet of octane on the rough surface?
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] A. 134°
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] B. 129°
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] C. 139°
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] D. 124°
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
