[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 问题: In a parallel universe where a magnet can have an isolated North or South pole, Maxwell’s equations look different. But, specifically, which of those equations are different?
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] A. The one related to the divergence of the magnetic field.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] B. The one related to the circulation of the magnetic field and the flux of the electric field.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] C. The ones related to the circulation of the electric field and the divergence of the magnetic field.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] D. The ones related to the divergence and the curl of the magnetic field.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Please select the correct answer and provide the final option letter and its corresponding content.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] In our conventional universe, Maxwell’s equations include the fact that magnetic monopoles do not exist, established by the equation:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \nabla \cdot \mathbf{B} = 0
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] This equation states that the magnetic field \(\mathbf{B}\) has zero divergence, implying no isolated magnetic charges.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] If in a parallel universe magnetic monopoles exist, this equation changes to include a magnetic charge density \(\rho_m\):
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \nabla \cdot \mathbf{B} = \rho_m
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Therefore, the equation related to the divergence of the magnetic field is different.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Also, the Maxwell-Faraday equation (curl of \(\mathbf{E}\)) remains the same, but the Ampère-Maxwell law (curl of \(\mathbf{B}\)) gets an added term to account for magnetic currents if magnetic monopoles exist, affecting the curl of \(\mathbf{B}\).
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Hence, the divergence and the curl of the magnetic field equations are different in the presence of magnetic monopoles.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Looking at the options:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] A. The one related to the divergence of the magnetic field. (Partly correct, but misses curl)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] B. The one related to the circulation of the magnetic field and the flux of the electric field. (The circulation of the magnetic field refers to curl of B; the flux of the electric field is divergence of E, so only partial.)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] C. The ones related to the circulation of the electric field and the divergence of the magnetic field. (Curl of E and div of B; curl of E is not changed by magnetic monopoles.)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] D. The ones related to the divergence and the curl of the magnetic field. (Both divergence and curl of B equations change, this is most accurate.)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Therefore, the correct answer is:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] D. The ones related to the divergence and the curl of the magnetic field.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
