[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Goal: Explore the relationship between chromatin structure and gene expression in patient cells compared to healthy cells.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Chromatin structure: Refers to how DNA is organized, including histone modifications, DNA accessibility, and 3D conformation.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Gene expression: Measuring the RNA produced from genes.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Methods:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 1. ChIP-seq (Chromatin Immunoprecipitation sequencing): Used to study protein-DNA interactions, including histone modifications and transcription factor binding. This gives information about chromatin state and regulation.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 2. RNA-seq (RNA sequencing): Measures gene expression genome-wide.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 3. qRT-PCR (quantitative reverse transcription PCR): Highly sensitive method to validate and quantify gene expression for specific genes.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 4. Chromosome conformation capture (such as 3C, Hi-C): Used to study 3D chromatin structure and long-range DNA interactions.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Now checking options:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] A. ChIP-seq and RNA-seq
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - ChIP-seq will give chromatin structure insights.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - RNA-seq will give gene expression on a broad scale.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - This combination can provide good information on chromatin state and expression.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] B. ChIP-seq, RNA-seq, and qRT PCR
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Adds qRT-PCR for validation of RNA-seq results.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - This combination is even more comprehensive for expression analysis and chromatin structure.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] C. Chromosome conformation capture and RNA-seq
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Chromosome conformation capture gives 3D chromatin structure.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - RNA-seq gives gene expression.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - This combination captures chromatin folding and expression, but no information on histone modifications or protein-DNA interactions.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] D. ChIP-seq, chromosome conformation capture, and qRT-PCR
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Combines histone/protein-DNA interaction data, 3D chromatin structure, and validation of gene expression via qRT-PCR.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - However, no genome-wide expression data like RNA-seq, which is useful for broader expression analysis.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Given the goal is to investigate chromatin structure and gene expression differences between patient and healthy cells, the best combination should include methods addressing both chromatin marks and gene expression.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Option B (ChIP-seq, RNA-seq, and qRT PCR) provides chromatin structure info and genome-wide expression plus expression validation, which is the most thorough and practical approach.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Option D omits RNA-seq, so lacks broad expression data, which is a limitation.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Therefore, the best choice is:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] B. CHIP-seq, RNA-seq, and qRT PCR
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
