[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] P_x = \frac{\hbar}{2} \sigma_x, \quad P_y = \frac{\hbar}{2} \sigma_y, \quad P_z = \frac{\hbar}{2} \sigma_z
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ---
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] **Step 1: Define the operator along \(\vec{n}\) direction**
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \(\vec{n}\) lies in the x-z plane, so \(\vec{n} = (\sin \theta, 0, \cos \theta)\)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Then the operator along \(\vec{n}\) is:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] P_n = \vec{P} \cdot \vec{n} = P_x \sin \theta + P_y \cdot 0 + P_z \cos \theta = P_x \sin \theta + P_z \cos \theta
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Substitute the matrices:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] P_n = \frac{\hbar}{2} \left(\sigma_x \sin \theta + \sigma_z \cos \theta \right)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ---
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] **Step 2: Form the explicit matrix for \(P_n\)**
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Recall:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \sigma_x = \begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\ 1 & 0\end{pmatrix}, \quad
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \sigma_z = \begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 0 & -1\end{pmatrix}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] So,
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] P_n = \frac{\hbar}{2}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \begin{pmatrix}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos \theta & \sin \theta \\
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \sin \theta & -\cos \theta
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \end{pmatrix}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ---
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] **Step 3: Find eigenvector corresponding to eigenvalue \(+\frac{\hbar}{2}\)**
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] We want to solve:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] P_n \psi = \frac{\hbar}{2} \psi
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Divide both sides by \(\frac{\hbar}{2}\):
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \begin{pmatrix}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos \theta & \sin \theta \\
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \sin \theta & -\cos \theta
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \end{pmatrix}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \begin{pmatrix}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] a \\
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] b
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \end{pmatrix}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] = 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \begin{pmatrix}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] a \\
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] b
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \end{pmatrix}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] This leads to a system:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos \theta \cdot a + \sin \theta \cdot b = a
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \sin \theta \cdot a - \cos \theta \cdot b = b
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Rewrite:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 1) \(\cos \theta \, a + \sin \theta \, b = a\)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \(\Rightarrow \cos \theta \, a + \sin \theta \, b - a = 0\)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \(\Rightarrow (\cos \theta -1) a + \sin \theta \, b = 0\)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 2) \(\sin \theta \, a - \cos \theta \, b = b\)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \(\Rightarrow \sin \theta \, a - \cos \theta \, b - b = 0\)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \(\Rightarrow \sin \theta \, a - (\cos \theta +1) b = 0\)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ---
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] **Step 4: Solve for ratio \(b/a\)**
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] From eq(1):
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] (\cos \theta -1) a + \sin \theta \, b = 0 \implies \sin \theta \, b = (1 - \cos \theta) a
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \Rightarrow b = a \frac{1 - \cos \theta}{\sin \theta}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] From eq(2):
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \sin \theta \, a = (\cos \theta + 1) b
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Substitute \(b\) from above:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \sin \theta \, a = (\cos \theta +1) a \frac{1 - \cos \theta}{\sin \theta}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Multiply both sides by \(\sin \theta\):
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \sin^2 \theta \, a = (\cos \theta +1)(1 - \cos \theta) a = (1 - \cos^2 \theta)a = \sin^2 \theta \, a
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] This confirms our solution is consistent.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ---
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] **Step 5: Simplify the ratio**
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Recall the half-angle formulas:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 1 - \cos \theta = 2 \sin^2 \frac{\theta}{2}, \quad \sin \theta = 2 \sin \frac{\theta}{2} \cos \frac{\theta}{2}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] So,
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \frac{1 - \cos \theta}{\sin \theta} = \frac{2 \sin^2 \frac{\theta}{2}}{2 \sin \frac{\theta}{2} \cos \frac{\theta}{2}} = \frac{\sin \frac{\theta}{2}}{\cos \frac{\theta}{2}} = \tan \frac{\theta}{2}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Hence,
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \frac{b}{a} = \tan \frac{\theta}{2}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ---
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] **Step 6: Write the eigenvector**
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Choose normalization such that:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \psi = \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix} = a \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ \tan \frac{\theta}{2} \end{pmatrix}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Normalize:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] |a|^2 \left( 1 + \tan^2 \frac{\theta}{2} \right) = 1 \implies |a| = \frac{1}{\sqrt{1 + \tan^2 \frac{\theta}{2}}} = \cos \frac{\theta}{2}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Thus:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \psi = \begin{pmatrix}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos \frac{\theta}{2} \\
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \sin \frac{\theta}{2}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \end{pmatrix}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ---
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] **Step 7: Compare with given options**
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Option C is:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] (\cos(\theta/2), \sin (\theta/2))
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] This matches the obtained normalized eigenvector.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ---
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
