[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] V -> CT: 13.2%
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] CV -> CT: 6.4 %
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Scientist 1 questioned the data, asking, "Why was the addition of V -> CT and CV -> CT (13.2% + 6.4%) greater than the m.u. for V -> CV (18.5%)?
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] A. Erred loci placement
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] B. The gene order was reversed
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] C. A double crossover event
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] D. Recombinant interference
