[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 问题: A coating is applied to a substrate resulting in a perfectly smooth surface. The measured contact angles of this smooth coating are 127° and 96° for water and oil respectively. The coating formulation is then modified and when now applied to the same type of substrate, a rough surface is produced. When a droplet of water or oil sits on the rough surface, pockets of air are now trapped in the cavities between the surface and the droplet. The droplets on the rough surface are now effectively in contact with 47% coating and 53% air. What would the measured water and oil contact angles of the rough surface be?
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] A. Water = 140°, Oil = 118°
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] B. Water = 144°, Oil = 125°
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] C. Water = 148°, Oil = 131°
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] D. Water = 151°, Oil = 136°
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Please select the correct answer and provide the final option letter and its corresponding content.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Given data:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Smooth surface contact angles:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85]   - Water, \( \theta_W = 127^\circ \)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85]   - Oil, \( \theta_O = 96^\circ \)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Rough surface composition under the droplet:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85]   - 47% coating (solid)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85]   - 53% air (trapped pockets)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] The problem involves wetting on a rough surface where the droplet contacts a composite surface of solid and air. This is described by the Cassie-Baxter equation for apparent contact angle \( \theta^* \):
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos \theta^* = f_s \cos \theta + (1 - f_s) \cos \theta_{air}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] where:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - \( f_s \) = fraction of solid surface in contact with liquid (47% = 0.47)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - \( \theta \) = intrinsic contact angle on the smooth solid surface
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - \( \theta_{air} \) = contact angle on air, which is \(180^\circ\) (since the droplet does not wet air)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - \( \cos 180^\circ = -1 \)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Calculate for water:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos \theta^*_W = 0.47 \cos 127^\circ + 0.53 \cos 180^\circ
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Calculate each term:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos 127^\circ = \cos (180^\circ - 53^\circ) = -\cos 53^\circ \approx -0.6018
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos 180^\circ = -1
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Thus:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos \theta^*_W = 0.47 \times (-0.6018) + 0.53 \times (-1) = -0.2828 - 0.53 = -0.8128
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Now, find \( \theta^*_W \):
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \theta^*_W = \cos^{-1} (-0.8128) \approx 144.6^\circ
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Calculate for oil:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos \theta^*_O = 0.47 \cos 96^\circ + 0.53 \cos 180^\circ
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Calculate each term:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos 96^\circ = \cos (90^\circ + 6^\circ) = -\sin 6^\circ \approx -0.1045
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos 180^\circ = -1
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Thus:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \cos \theta^*_O = 0.47 \times (-0.1045) + 0.53 \times (-1) = -0.0491 - 0.53 = -0.5791
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Now, find \( \theta^*_O \):
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \theta^*_O = \cos^{-1} (-0.5791) \approx 125.4^\circ
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
