[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ### Step 1: Hydrogenation with Pd/C of limonene, stopping at 1 equivalent of H2
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - One equivalent of hydrogen will partially hydrogenate only one of the alkenes (likely the more reactive one).
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The typical Pd/C hydrogenation reduces the exocyclic alkene faster than the internal one.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Result: The exocyclic double bond is hydrogenated to an isopropyl group attached to the ring.
