[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ### Step 3: Treatment of product 2 with sodium methoxide (NaOMe)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Sodium methoxide is a nucleophile that will open the epoxide.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Under basic conditions, the epoxide opening occurs via nucleophilic attack at the less hindered position with inversion of configuration.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The ring epoxide will open with attack of methoxide (MeO-) to form a trans-1,2-methoxy alcohol.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The alkoxide oxygen will get protonated during work-up, so product 3 is a methoxy alcohol.
