[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Step 1: Identify the starting compound and reagents.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Starting compound: methyl isoamyl ketone. This is a ketone with an isoamyl group and a methyl group attached. Isoamyl refers to 3-methylbutyl.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Reagents: hydrogen peroxide (H2O2) and boron trifluoride (BF3) in diethyl ether.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Step 2: Understand the reaction.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Ketones treated with H2O2 and BF3 often undergo Baeyer-Villiger oxidation.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Baeyer-Villiger oxidation inserts an oxygen atom next to the carbonyl carbon, converting ketones into esters.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85]   
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Step 3: Write the structure and product.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Methyl isoamyl ketone is something like this:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] O
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ||
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] CH3–C–(isoamyl)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] The isoamyl group is 3-methylbutyl: (CH3-CH2-CH(CH3)-CH2-)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] But to be more exact, methyl isoamyl ketone is also known as 4-methylpentan-2-one.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Structure:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] CH3-CO-CH2-CH2-CH(CH3)2
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Wait, isoamyl usually refers to (CH3)2CH-CH2-CH2- (3-methylbutyl). So the ketone is CH3-CO-CH2-CH2-CH(CH3)2, with the methyl on the 4th carbon.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Generally "methyl isoamyl ketone" means 4-methylpentan-2-one:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] CH3-CO-CH2-CH2-CH(CH3)2
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Step 4: Baeyer-Villiger oxidation of this ketone.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - BV oxidation inserts an oxygen next to the carbonyl, forming an ester.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The migration preference for BV oxidation: tertiary > secondary > primary alkyl groups.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The groups attached to the carbonyl are: methyl and isoamyl (a primary or secondary alkyl group? Isoamyl is 3-methylbutyl, which is a primary or secondary?)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Looking carefully, the groups attached to the carbonyl are methyl and 3-methylbutyl.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Between methyl (CH3-) and 3-methylbutyl (CH3-CH2-CH(CH3)-CH2-), the bulkier group (3-methylbutyl) will migrate.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] So, the oxygen inserts between the carbonyl carbon and the 3-methylbutyl group, forming an ester:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] CH3-C(=O)-R → CH3-C(=O)-O-R (ester)
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] where R = 3-methylbutyl.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Step 5: Product structure:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Methyl 3-methylbutanoate
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
