[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] **Goal:** Identify which compound contains the most electronically deshielded hydrogen nucleus (i.e., which hydrogen experiences the greatest downfield shift in NMR due to electronic effects).
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ---
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ### Step 1: Understand "electronically deshielded hydrogen"
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - In NMR, **deshielding** of a proton's nucleus occurs when electron density around it is decreased, typically by electron-withdrawing groups nearby.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Electronegative substituents near a hydrogen pull electron density away, increasing the local magnetic field felt by the nucleus - causing a downfield shift (higher ppm).
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The more electron-withdrawing or electronegative the substituent close to the proton in question, the more deshielding.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ---
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ### Step 2: Consider the groups and their effects
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] The position is 7 on bicyclo[2.2.1]heptane: an exo- or endo-position at the bridgehead.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - **Fluorine (F)** is highly electronegative, strong electron-withdrawing inductively.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - **Difluoro (two fluorines)** is even more electron withdrawing than one fluorine.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - **Methoxy (–OCH3)** is generally electron donating by resonance but slightly electron withdrawing inductively.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] - **Propan-2-ylidene (isopropylidene group = an alkene substituent)** mainly is a neutral or donating group, not strongly electron withdrawing.
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] For the proton closest to the substituent, the greatest electronic deshielding will be expected when the substituent is the most electron withdrawing and close by.
