[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Thus,
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] (nSi/nFe)_1 = 10^{0.3} ≈ 2.0
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Rearranged:
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] nSi_1 = 2.0 × nFe_1
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Also, from above,
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] log10(nFe/nH)_1 = -4.5 => nFe_1 = 10^{-4.5}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] Therefore,
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] nSi_1 = 2.0 × 10^{-4.5} = 2.0 × 3.1623 × 10^{-5} ≈ 6.32 × 10^{-5}
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:35:58 run_experiments_1.py:85] ---
