[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] - \(aH\) is a left coset of \(H\) in \(G\).
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] - \(Ha\) is a right coset of \(H\) in \(G\).
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The size of a left coset \(aH\) is equal to the size of \(H\), and similarly the size of any right coset \(Ha\) is also equal to \(|H|\).
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Therefore, \(|aH| = |H| = |Ha|\).
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] So, **Statement 1 is true**.
