[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Typically, left cosets form a partition of \(G\), and right cosets form a separate partition of \(G\).
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The intersection between a left coset and a right coset can be non-empty without the two cosets being identical (since they are different in that one is left coset and the other is a right coset).
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] - Hence, the statement that \(aH\) and \(Hb\) are identical or disjoint is **false**.
