[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] ### Step 2: Find the order of the element \((1,1)\)
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] The order of the element \((1,1)\) in the direct product group is the least common multiple (LCM) of the orders of \(1 \in \mathbb{Z}_{11}\) and \(1 \in \mathbb{Z}_{15}\).
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The order of \(1 \in \mathbb{Z}_{11}\) is 11 (since 11 is prime and 1 generates it).
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] - The order of \(1 \in \mathbb{Z}_{15}\) is 15 (since 1 generates the whole \(\mathbb{Z}_{15}\)).
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] So, the order of \((1,1)\) is:
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
