[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] ### Step 3: Determine the subgroup generated by \((1,1)\)
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] Since the order of \((1,1)\) is 165, the subgroup \(\langle (1,1) \rangle\) has order 165 and is a cyclic subgroup of order 165 inside \(\mathbb{Z}_{11} \times \mathbb{Z}_{15}\).
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] ### Step 4: Find the factor group order
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] The order of the factor group \((\mathbb{Z}_{11} \times \mathbb{Z}_{15}) / \langle (1,1) \rangle\) is:
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \frac{| \mathbb{Z}_{11} \times \mathbb{Z}_{15} |}{| \langle (1,1) \rangle |} = \frac{165}{165} = 1.
