[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] Key properties under multiplication:
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 1. **Closure**: The product of any two nth roots of unity is also an nth root of unity.
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 2. **Associativity**: Multiplication of complex numbers is associative.
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 3. **Identity**: The element \( e^{2\pi i \cdot 0/n} = 1 \) acts as the identity element.
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 4. **Inverses**: Every nth root of unity has an inverse, which is its complex conjugate in this set because \( (e^{2\pi i k/n})^{-1} = e^{-2\pi i k/n} = e^{2\pi i (n-k)/n} \), which is also an nth root of unity.
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 5. **Commutativity**: Multiplication of complex numbers is commutative.
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] From these points, the set of nth roots of unity under multiplication forms a group that is also abelian (commutative).
