[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] ### Step 3: Check if \(f(x)\) factors into irreducible polynomials of degree 1 and 2
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] For \(c=2\), since no roots, linear factorization is impossible. Could it factor into the product of two polynomials of degrees 1 and 2? That would mean:
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] f(x) = (x + a)(x^2 + b x + d)
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] for some \(a,b,d \in \mathbb{Z}_3\).
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] Multiply:
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] (x + a)(x^2 + b x + d) = x^3 + b x^2 + d x + a x^2 + a b x + a d = x^3 + (b + a) x^2 + (d + a b) x + a d
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] Match with \(f(x) = x^3 + x^2 + 2\):
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \begin{cases}
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] b + a = 1 \\
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] d + a b = 0 \\
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] a d = 2
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \end{cases}
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] Try all \(a \in \{0,1,2\}\):
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] - If \(a=0\):
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] b + 0 = 1 \implies b=1
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] d + 0 =0 \implies d=0
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 0 \cdot d=0 \neq 2
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] No.
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] - If \(a=1\):
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] b + 1 =1 \implies b=0
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] d + 1 \cdot 0 = d + 0 = 0 \implies d=0
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 1 \cdot d = 1 \cdot 0=0 \neq 2
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] No.
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] - If \(a=2\):
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] b + 2 =1 \implies b=1 - 2 = -1 \equiv 2
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] d + 2 \times 2 = d + 4 = d + 1 = 0 \implies d=2
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \[
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] a d = 2 \times 2 = 4 \equiv 1 \neq 2
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] \]
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] No.
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] No \(a\) yields \(a d = 2\).
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] Thus no factorization into degree 1 and 2 polynomials.
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] 
[INFO] 10-07 19:43:56 run_experiments_1.py:85] ---
